<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 1.65 bln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 1.65 bln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 1.65 billion stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>It allotted 329 million stg outright in bills and 1.321 billion in repos to August 13 and 14.</p>
<p>The Bank has now provided liquidity totalling 2.854 billion stg so far on Thursday, in response to a revised money market shortage forecast of 2.85 billion stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
